{"title": "Someone rebuilt old Android versions in your browser, and it’s an instant nostalgia hit [Gallery]", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/16/android-time-machine-old-versions-browser/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2021/06/android_figure_developer_1.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The “Android Time Machine” is a fun project that puts Android versions into your browser, giving you a quick and easy chance to play around with older versions for a quick hit of nostalgia.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/16/android-time-machine-old-versions-browser/#more-737679\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-16T06:40:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-17T19:03:01.972523+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Google’s Intelligent Eyewear glasses from Gentle Monster are already sold out", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/16/google-intelligent-eyewear-gentle-monster-android-xr-sold-out/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/android-xr-intelligent-eyewear-gentle-monster-15.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One of the first partner brands selling Android XR glasses, “Intelligent Eyewear” as Google calls it, has already completely sold out, with Gentle Monster no longer accepting pre-orders just days after launch.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/16/google-intelligent-eyewear-gentle-monster-android-xr-sold-out/#more-737678\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-16T06:10:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-17T19:03:01.972523+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Save serious money with RedPocket Mobile’s $5 Black Friday plans", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/16/save-serious-money-with-redpockets-black-friday-plans-that-start-at-5-a-month-sponsored/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/00947cc8ee4c3fe022e46888fd9a63f8_abt-us-mob.webp?w=1536\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You’re not going to believe this, but there’s one part of your life that’s not actually getting more expensive. If you <a href=\"https://www.redpocket.com/shop?utm_source=9to5&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=9to5_article\" rel=\"sponsored nofollow\">switch to RedPocket Mobile</a> during its Black Friday sale, you can ditch your costly carrier and get a plan that starts at $5 per month. It’s not too good to be true: RedPocket has been around for 20 years, and unlike most MVNOs, it’s independently owned and operated. That gives it the ability to offer you real network choice when you sign up for a new plan (we’ll explain more later), and keeps your costs low. Really low.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/16/save-serious-money-with-redpockets-black-friday-plans-that-start-at-5-a-month-sponsored/#more-735678\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-16T06:01:55+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-17T19:03:01.972523+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Google Maps rolling out travel itineraries & list search for Ask Maps", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/16/google-ask-maps-itineraries/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/Google-Ask-Maps-plans-cover.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Ahead of the holiday season, Google Maps is launching a handy travel itineraries feature alongside a slew of other new capabilities for Ask Maps.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/16/google-ask-maps-itineraries/#more-737258\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-16T05:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-17T19:03:01.972523+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Pixel Tag is a brilliant Band-Aid on a Find Hub network Google can’t easily fix", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/15/google-pixel-tag-find-hub-problems/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/google-pixel-tag-8.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The Google Pixel Tag is here and, at least so far, it’s really good. But fresh hardware and some new features can’t fix the core problem. Google’s Find Hub network has been restricted from the very start, and it’s not something Google can easily fix.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left wp-block-paragraph\"><em>9to5Google Weekender by Ben Schoon is a part of our free newsletter that also includes ‘Inbox,’ a twice-weekly roundup of key stories from around the web by Daniel Bader. <a href=\"https://9to5google.beehiiv.com/subscribe\">Sign up here</a> to get Weekender delivered to your inbox every Sunday along with ‘Inbox’ on Tuesday and Thursday. <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/feature/newsletter/\">You can find past issues here</a>.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Sign up below to access the web version.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/15/google-pixel-tag-find-hub-problems/#more-736450\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-15T05:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-17T19:03:01.972523+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Google Pixel rolls out new ‘Family Hub’ feature with useful controls [Gallery]", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/14/google-pixel-family-hub-feature-rolled-out/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/09/Pixel-11-Pro-camera-close-up.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">First <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/03/google-android-family-hub-feature/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">appearing</a> earlier this month, Google Pixel phones are rolling out a handy new Family feature in the Settings menu. Here’s what it can do.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/14/google-pixel-family-hub-feature-rolled-out/#more-737539\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-14T14:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-17T19:03:01.972523+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Pixel 11 Pro’s HiLight feature also now works on WhatsApp messages", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/13/pixel-11-pro-hilight-whatsapp/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/08/Pixel-11-Pro-Hilight-Phone-Call.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">After being barebones at launch, Google is improving on Pixel 11 Pro’s Hilight feature with message support, now including WhatsApp.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/13/pixel-11-pro-hilight-whatsapp/#more-737533\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-13T16:15:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-17T19:03:01.972523+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Pixelated 125: Google’s glasses, Meta’s baggage", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/13/pixelated-125-googles-glasses-metas-baggage/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2024/03/Pixelated-cover.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Welcome to Pixelated episode 125. This week, <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/google-glasses-hands-on/\">Abner has tried out</a> Google’s new lineup of “Intelligent Eyewear,” and he’s got plenty to share with Damien and Will. Can Google nail the smart glasses experience while <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/12/google-android-xr-glasses-camera-privacy/\">digging itself out of a privacy hole</a> Meta first dug? For as much work as the company’s doing, only time might tell.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Enjoy the show? You can listen to our weekly members-only Pixelated Pro bonus episode by <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/pro/\">signing up for 9to5Google Pro</a> for just $5 per month, or about $1 per episode.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Sponsored by Proton Unlimited</strong>: Pixelated listeners can save 30% on an annual subscription to the company’s suite of privacy-friendly services by <a href=\"https://proton.me/9to5google\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">signing up using our link</a>. Thanks to Proton Unlimited for sponsoring the podcast.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio controls=\"controls\" src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/pix125.mp3\"></audio></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-subscribe\">Subscribe</h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLcKP282Ii48tKK_KUt1kq1Ist9FkYR6lO\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">YouTube Podcasts</a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://pca.st/podcast/ac8e6ce0-06b1-0136-c264-7d73a919276a\" rel